To generate a table of contents (TOC) automatically in a LaTeX document, you can use the following commands:

1. Add the `toc` option to the document class in the preamble:

```latex
\documentclass[toc]{article}
```

This will include the `toc` package, which provides the necessary commands for generating the TOC.

2. Add the `\tableofcontents` command where you want the TOC to appear in your document:

```latex
\begin{document}
  \tableofcontents
  ...
```

This will generate the TOC based on the `\section`, `\subsection`, `\subsubsection`, and other sectioning commands used in your document.

3. Use the sectioning commands (e.g., `\section`, `\subsection`, etc.) to structure your document:

```latex
\section{Introduction}
...
\subsection{Background}
...
\subsubsection{History}
...
\section{Methods}
...
\subsection{Participants}
...
\subsubsection{Materials}
...
\end{document}
```

The TOC will automatically include the section titles and their respective levels.

Here's an example of a complete LaTeX document with a generated TOC:

```latex
\documentclass[toc]{article}

\begin{document}
  \tableofcontents

  \section{Introduction}
    ...

  \subsection{Background}
    ...

  \subsubsection{History}
    ...

  \section{Methods}
    ...

  \subsection{Participants}
    ...

  \subsubsection{Materials}
    ...

\end{document}
```

This will produce a TOC that looks like this:

```
Contents
1. Introduction
2. Background
   2.1 History
3. Methods
   3.1 Participants
   3.2 Materials
```

